title: 'SyncGuard: reports shell $? for native libgit2 push failures + dies in DESTROY'
updated: 2026-07-02T16:12:06Z
---

SyncGuard.pm:88 says "git push failed (exit code $?)" but native Git::Native
ops set no shell exit code (Git.pm:50-55 documents last_error as the channel);
the message is factually wrong. Additionally die inside DESTROY can mask the
original exception and may be swallowed during global destruction — prefer
warn + distinct signaling. Found during architecture sweep. VERSION 0.304.
Fixed in 7c574b3: SyncGuard DESTROY now uses $git->last_error (native libgit2 has no shell $?) and warns instead of die() (die during unwind gets swallowed as '(in cleanup)'). Regression test t/50-syncguard-errors.t; full suite green (306 tests).
Landed on main as 6d48ce0 (cherry-pick + Changes entry). Follow-up bug (guard discarded in void context, insurance never engages) filed as #28.
